    {
      "finding": "A regular file reached through a symlinked source ancestor was accepted.",
      "resolution": "regular_file rejects every symbolic-link component and verifies containment for both inputs and generated outputs. File/ancestor/output-symlink probes reject all three cases."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Generated outputs and PASS reports could be accidentally marked buildInput and produce a stale success receipt.",
      "resolution": "Build seeds are restricted to source/proof prefixes and suffixes, and disjoint from generated paths, audit paths and reserved log/receipt paths. The actual 31-file seed list has 27 Python/JavaScript code files and 4 proof texts, with no generated IR, table or report."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Inherited PYTHONOPTIMIZE could disable assertion-based audits while allowing PASS output.",
      "resolution": "An optimized wrapper invocation is rejected; PYTHONOPTIMIZE is also removed from the child environment. An additional python-E probe verifies the environment removal rather than relying only on the wrapper debug guard."
    },
