  "codeReview": [
    "Explicit outputs must be absent or empty and outside the proposal source directory. Nonempty-output probes preserve the existing sentinel byte for byte. The default uses a newly created temporary directory under the repository build directory.",
    "Source and expected-output manifests reject noncanonical or escaping paths, duplicate entries, malformed hashes and byte counts, missing required bindings, and empty output/audit/table lists. The wrapper and expected-output manifest themselves are source-manifest-bound.",
    "The staged construction entry point calls every build/check command with check=True. The wrapper propagates any child failure, requires the final success marker, compares declared byte lengths and SHA256 values, compares the committed table bytes, requires successful audit statuses, and rechecks source files plus the source-manifest digest after execution.",
    "A receipt is written only after every preceding check succeeds. Missing markers, failed statuses, missing reports, mismatched generated artifacts or committed tables, and changed source files/manifests all reject in isolated probes.",
    "The actual staged inventory had 105 declared files plus SOURCE_MANIFEST.json, no missing/unlisted files and no symlinks at review. All 31 build-input hashes match the approved source/proof files. The 51 expected outputs and selected table summary match the completed reference build; all 14 required reference reports record successful status.",
    "The manifest explicitly excludes 7 timing-dependent whole-file comparisons while preserving their generation and mathematical checks. The zero-operation final elimination certificate is independently replayed by run_pipeline.py and again by verify_package.py; it is not trusted merely because its volatile bytes are excluded.",
    "The README accurately distinguishes construction reproduction from PDF rendering and states the conditional inherited-global boundary. This review finds no remaining overwrite, stale-seed, failure-propagation, or reproducibility-claim blocker in the reviewed code and manifest."
  ],
